19\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Problem_21\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 21</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Problem_22\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 22</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">23</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-24\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">24</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-25\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">25</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-26\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">26</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c3256ece2a6e21e4fa740b3cb9d3b2e22da6da72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{10} + \\dfrac{9}{100} + \\dfrac{9}{1000} + \\dfrac{7}{10000} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"228\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcff57155768e03c7fad58eea05616960246e14b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 0.0026 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 0.0197 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 0.1997 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 0.26 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 1.997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"510\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ahn chooses a two-digit integer, subtracts it from 200, and doubles the result.  What is the largest number Ahn can get?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/e/c5e803237273c3e26924c3bc273b6c8bcc70ca66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 200 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 202 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 220 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 380 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 398$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following numbers is the largest?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d615d345b747ad9863024c905f510fa13c28754e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 0.97 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 0.979 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 0.9709 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 0.907 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 0.9089$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"500\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Julie is preparing a speech for her class.  Her speech must last between one-half hour and three-quarters of an hour.  The ideal rate of speech is 150 words per minute.  If Julie speaks at the ideal rate, which of the following number of words would be an appropriate length for her speech?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/928a2bfb4b36243537507623db7b0536caaf7a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 2250 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 3000 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 4200 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 4350 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 5650$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"466\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are many two-digit multiples of 7, but only two of the multiples have a digit sum of 10.  The sum of these two multiples of 7 is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/51674d58b4d21a29220b03914afaf3924e747e5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 119 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 126 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 140 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 175 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 189$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/4081a599cf6570a3bdf24c89b9c4fbf79bd51f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$74982.1035$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> the value of the <i>place</i> occupied by the digit 9 is how many times as great as the value of the <i>place</i> occupied by the digit 3?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8753e0798ee304d3ae572657187b78689be1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 1,000 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 10,000 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 100,000 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 1,000,000 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 10,000,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"614\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the smallest square that will contain a circle of radius 4 is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2ded86b6302d8403bb6c953331fc44103cd5a151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 16 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 32 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 64 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 128$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Walter gets up at 6:30 a.m., catches the school bus at 7:30 a.m., has 6 classes that last 50 minutes each, has 30 minutes for lunch, and has 2 hours additional time at school.  He takes the bus home and arrives at 4:00 p.m.  How many minutes has he spent on the bus?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3261d38c975cc2191dc5591a022c023bf7caa8a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 60 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 75 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 90 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"384\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three students, with different names, line up in single file.  What is the probability that they are in alphabetical order from front-to-back?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f2367dec20964321df8ad6fd561fa193fdcdaae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{12} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{9} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{6} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"358\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What fraction of this square region is shaded?  Stripes are equal in width, and the figure is drawn to scale.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86c93e913025a304bc6292d9f589f70d95dda2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(8); fill((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,6)--(0,6)--cycle,black); fill((0,0)--(5,0)--(5,5)--(0,5)--cycle,white); fill((0,0)--(4,0)--(4,4)--(0,4)--cycle,black); fill((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle,white); fill((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle,black); fill((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle,white); draw((0,6)--(0,0)--(6,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"82\" height=\"82\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b99b42fac44c99cb409701fc24891d956697328b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{12} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{2} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{7}{12} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{3} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a79db58adaa5ede8cc761cfcb0465f8726f22a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"28\" height=\"24\" /> as the number of whole number divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.  For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9dfc8f931da505cfd67e4c8dc260314ab7549d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{3}=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"23\" /> because 3 has two divisors, 1 and 3.  Find the value of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e99d4be60abd970bb4dfbcb2c45c014f0ecc3be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\boxed{11}\\times\\boxed{20}}.\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80bd28708cfd1c2e8c2d707650650747f5f97cf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 16 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"358\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f14169c284e3892bc75537b563f01a5b975ac61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle 1 + \\angle 2 = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/54205ed43c0badda2d6690614c3b2e98d0affced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle 3 = \\angle 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/024779d698ce7fe0551444a32dce168e990ee4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f0cab5df9bf98e5c9cd3ffe8661ec2772becc8f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair H,I,J,K,L; H = (0,0); I = 10*dir(70); J = I + 10*dir(290); K = J + 5*dir(110); L = J + 5*dir(0); draw(H--I--J--cycle); draw(K--L--J); draw(arc((0,0),dir(70),(1,0),CW)); label(&quot;$70^\\circ$&quot;,dir(35),NE); draw(arc(I,I+dir(250),I+dir(290),CCW)); label(&quot;$40^\\circ$&quot;,I+1.25*dir(270),S); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,J+0.25*dir(162.5),NW); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,J+0.25*dir(17.5),NE); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,L+dir(162.5),WNW); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,K+dir(-52.5),SE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"202\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95b5dd0db0db91ea4c885108512c90c49259fa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 20^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 25^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 30^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 35^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 40^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"412\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three bags of jelly beans contain 26, 28, and 30 beans.  The ratios of yellow beans to all beans in each of these bags are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, respectively.  All three bags of candy are dumped into one bowl.  Which of the following is closest to the ratio of yellow jelly beans to all beans in the bowl?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107649e9eb183f1327c669f618b37a9f567cb004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 31\\% \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 32\\% \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 33\\% \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 35\\% \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 95\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"454\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is a set of five positive integers whose average (mean) is 5, whose median is 5, and whose only mode is 8.  What is the difference between the largest and smallest integers in the set?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd2ca7ce011b71e53caa98889fff803fd5d40df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each side of the large square in the figure is trisected (divided into three equal parts).  The corners of an inscribed square are at these trisection points, as shown.  The ratio of the area of the inscribed square to the area of the large square is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/9/f69a1c109464f1f5fc9c655bbee9a93db750e4e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle); draw((1,0)--(1,0.2)); draw((2,0)--(2,0.2)); draw((3,1)--(2.8,1)); draw((3,2)--(2.8,2)); draw((1,3)--(1,2.8)); draw((2,3)--(2,2.8)); draw((0,1)--(0.2,1)); draw((0,2)--(0.2,2)); draw((2,0)--(3,2)--(1,3)--(0,1)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f137dda89e944971994c3eaff173bb540a25c3e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{9} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{3} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{7}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"379\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Penni Precisely buys \\$100 worth of stock in each of three companies: Alabama Almonds, Boston Beans, and California Cauliflower.  After one year, AA was up 20%, BB was down 25%, and CC was unchanged.  For the second year, AA was down 20% from the previous year, BB was up 25% from the previous year, and CC was unchanged.  If A, B, and C are the final values of the stock, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b54c3f506d0161c7abc34f96381eae0784bc815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ A=B=C \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ A=B&lt;C \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ C&lt;B=A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"431\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca3ae88d71116381af82eb7dd4845a43ed97d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(D)}\\ A&lt;B&lt;C \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ B&lt;A&lt;C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"276\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A cube has eight vertices (corners) and twelve edges.  A segment, such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, which joins two vertices not joined by an edge is called a diagonal.  Segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is also a diagonal.  How many diagonals does a cube have?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0aacb382465f0de3a897e96bfd62a18e92607fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,3)--(0,0)--(3,0)--(5.5,1)--(5.5,4)--(3,3)--(0,3)--(2.5,4)--(5.5,4)); draw((3,0)--(3,3)); draw((0,0)--(2.5,1)--(5.5,1)--(0,3)--(5.5,4),dashed); draw((2.5,4)--(2.5,1),dashed); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(2.75,3.5),NNE); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(4.125,1.5),NNE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"185\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5b687a4edab9cdcce9462f4d2d9d214cf37216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 14 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the grocery store last week, small boxes of facial tissue were priced at 4 boxes for \\$5.  This week they are on sale at 5 boxes for \\$4.  The percent decrease in the price per box during the sale was closest to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95c9ad76cf91ec9c92f06669cc6fcf39f062366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 30\\% \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 35\\% \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 40\\% \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 45\\% \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 65\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"451\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/3178731c43a073a28b63adf2831b669ba2712b6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3}{2}\\cdot \\dfrac{4}{3}\\cdot \\dfrac{5}{4}\\cdot \\dfrac{6}{5}\\cdot \\ldots\\cdot \\dfrac{a}{b} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"188\" height=\"38\" />, what is the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a53bb4cd8a8a1e56aa5c9bf6657dbe129b092f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 11 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 13 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 17 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 35 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pair of 8-sided dice have sides numbered 1 through 8.  Each side has the same probability (chance) of landing face up.  The probability that the product of the two numbers that land face-up exceeds 36 is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fa7ad0ed51bbd85582d9b5d90c052471f6ae88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{32} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{11}{64} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{3}{16} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{4} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_21\">Problem 21</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 21\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each corner cube is removed from this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc88188559ffd8bb60070e46d4a3ea6aec061f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\text{ cm}\\times 3\\text{ cm}\\times 3\\text{ cm}$\" width=\"152\" height=\"12\" /> cube.  The surface area of the remaining figure is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6796b398e26ace16bbcb7742021e113487ac93bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((1.8,3.66)--(0,3)--(0,0)); draw((2.8,3.66)--(1,3)--(1,0)); draw((3.8,3.66)--(2,3)--(2,0)); draw((4.8,3.66)--(3,3)--(3,0));  draw((0,0)--(3,0)--(4.8,0.66)); draw((0,1)--(3,1)--(4.8,1.66)); draw((0,2)--(3,2)--(4.8,2.66)); draw((0,3)--(3,3)--(4.8,3.66));  draw((0,3)--(3,3)--(3,0)); draw((0.6,3.22)--(3.6,3.22)--(3.6,0.22)); draw((1.2,3.44)--(4.2,3.44)--(4.2,0.44)); draw((1.8,3.66)--(4.8,3.66)--(4.8,0.66)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a384a4cb92402742f2d41af51a582cbfe1190cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 19\\text{ sq.cm} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 24\\text{ sq.cm} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 30\\text{ sq.cm} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 54\\text{ sq.cm} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 72\\text{ sq.cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"609\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_22\">Problem 22</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 22\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A two-inch cube <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/9548c418c158a537d059200a27a14220f55b9c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\times 2\\times 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> of silver weighs 3 pounds and is worth \\$200.  How much is a three-inch cube of silver worth?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29ab3c117307ccac16226a3c9bf2185f06244013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 300\\text{ dollars} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 375\\text{ dollars} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 450\\text{ dollars} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 560\\text{ dollars} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 675\\text{ dollars}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"689\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are positive integers that have these properties:\n</p>\n<ul><li>the sum of the squares of their digits is 50, and</li>\n<li>each digit is larger than the one to its left.</li></ul>\n<p>The product of the digits of the largest integer with both properties is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/2724824318fca99ff7c440291b589afbdad9886a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 25 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 36 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 48 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is divided at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37bac8710233ca570649f0526e28b1a1ebb69d1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:3$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />.  The two semicircles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/b/c7bc69328ef74607767b467b2a851f202438edec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, divide the circular region into an upper (shaded) region and a lower region.  The ratio of the area of the upper region to that of the lower region is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4ecc539294cfbe2d303003a6f52d3bae65ada85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,EE; A = (0,0); B = (2,2); C = (4,0); D = (7,-3); EE = (10,0); fill(arc((2,0),A,C,CW)--arc((7,0),C,EE,CCW)--arc((5,0),EE,A,CCW)--cycle,gray); draw(arc((2,0),A,C,CW)--arc((7,0),C,EE,CCW)); draw(circle((5,0),5));  dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D); dot(EE); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,N); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,EE,W); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"225\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/0622fc94175079974df29516830b50670047c8d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 2:3 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 1:1 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 3:2 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 9:4 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 5:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"451\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All of the even numbers from 2 to 98 inclusive, excluding those ending in 0, are multiplied together.  What is the rightmost digit (the units digit) of the product?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51b559a448d96a31b842a6d199f60beb8583fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1997 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AJHSM